<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex details 1996 income, sales.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex details 1996 income, sales.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) reported its 1996 consolidated income statement. Figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>    Item				   1995		   1996</p>
<p>  Total Sales			   22,657		 22,820</p>
<p>  Domestic Sales			14,318		 17,217</p>
<p>  Export Sales			   8,339		 11,603</p>
<p>  Costs, Operating Expenses	  7,448		  8,167</p>
<p>Income before taxes, interests</p>
<p>   royalties, other expenses	15,209		 20,653</p>
<p>  Income before taxes, royalties  15,945		 21,065</p>
<p>  Taxes, Royalties		    14,362		 19,132</p>
<p>  Net Income			     1,583		  1,933</p>
<p>  Operating Income Before Taxes   12,991		 18,404</p>
<p>  Pemex Exploration &amp; Production  12,857		 18,651</p>
<p>  Pemex Refinacion		     (343)		  (322)</p>
<p>  Pemex Gas				  171		     27</p>
<p>  Pemex Petrochemicals		   306		     47</p>
<p>Legend: Statement is unaudited, *includes consumer taxes.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
